{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-7104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{t}^{2}-12t,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-7104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-12t) \\\\  & =6t-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=1,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\nv(1)=6(1)-12=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-6|=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-7104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41ac7d156f0da8ff91370983e82ed6aa85c922779df9b89bb8d92ec201c41e07"} {"question" "q-7104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-7104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-7104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-19302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{2}-2t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=3.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-19302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\  & =2t-2+\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=3,$ we substitute $t=3$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =2(3)-2+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =6-2+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3} \\\\  & =4.333\\,333… \\\\  & ≈4.33\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-19302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41ac7d156f0da8ff91370983e82ed6aa85c922779df9b89bb8d92ec201c41e07"} {"question" "q-19302" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-19302" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "v=0.22"] ["math" "v=3.75"] ["math" "v=4.33"] ["math" "v=6.67"] ["math" "v=8.05"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-19302" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "v=4.33"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-19308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in feet) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{e}^{-t}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-3t,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-19308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{e}^{-t}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-3t) \\\\  & =-3{e}^{-t}+\\frac{3}{t}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=3,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =-3{e}^{-3}+\\frac{3}{3}-3 \\\\  & =-3{e}^{-3}-2 \\\\  & ≈-2.15\\,\\text{ft/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-2.15|=2.15\\,\\text{ft/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-19308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41ac7d156f0da8ff91370983e82ed6aa85c922779df9b89bb8d92ec201c41e07"} {"question" "q-19308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-19308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.18\\,\\text{ft/s}"] ["math" "1.92\\,\\text{ft/s}"] ["math" "2.15\\,\\text{ft/s}"] ["math" "3.25\\,\\text{ft/s}"] ["math" "3.52\\,\\text{ft/s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-19308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2.15\\,\\text{ft/s}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-73136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1).$ Calculate the velocity at time $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-73136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The velocity is the derivative of the position function $x(t)$ with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-73136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41ac7d156f0da8ff91370983e82ed6aa85c922779df9b89bb8d92ec201c41e07"} {"question" "q-73136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-73136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "v(t)=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)}"] ["math" "v(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "v(t)=\\frac{2t}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)}"] ["math" "v(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "v(t)=\\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-73136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-336146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{log}_{2}⁡t-2t,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=2.$ Round your answer to one decimal place.\n\n$v(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-336146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{log}_{2}⁡t-2t) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =\\frac{3}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-2 \\\\  & =0.16404… \\\\  & ≈0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-336146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41ac7d156f0da8ff91370983e82ed6aa85c922779df9b89bb8d92ec201c41e07"} {"question" "q-336146" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"} {"question" "q-336146" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014243/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab2f422bf3e51bf8865ea872b0bbbf192dd7b4b829f2557c7fe459211b42d859"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1184 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
